From 72a37cf2c79caca47157dfbe06484b508332b65e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 00:47:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] CDVDDemuxFFmpeg: the count of HDR10+ without statistics
 emptied with the other maps of the probe

The second independent review of 1.0 RC6 (O-A3) found that
m_dvWithoutStatistics was not emptied in Dispose(), unlike the other
maps of ProbeHdr10Plus(): after a Reset() of the same file (Dispose and
Open), its count was added to the one before. The decision did not
change (the same stream), but the number that kodi.log gives was twice
what was looked at.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
index 96e22ab..ef7b297 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVDDemuxFFmpeg.cpp
@@ -804,6 +804,7 @@ void CDVDDemuxFFmpeg::Dispose()
   m_dvFromHdr10Plus.clear();
   m_dvHdrBefore.clear();
   m_dvMeasured.clear();
+  m_dvWithoutStatistics.clear(); // (Hades: as the other maps of ProbeHdr10Plus())
   m_dvNotJoined.clear();
 #endif
 
-- 
2.53.0

